# Production build settings. Committed on purpose -- this is configuration, not
# secrets, and every VITE_ variable ends up readable in the built JavaScript.
#
# Relative, because CloudFront serves the app and the API from one domain: the
# request is same-origin and needs no host.
#
# Defined here rather than passed on the command line so the value cannot be
# mangled by the shell. Passing VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api from Git Bash silently
# rewrites it to "C:/Program Files/Git/api" (MSYS path conversion), which
# builds and deploys cleanly and then fails in the browser with a network error.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
